[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TextureRect"]
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 112.0
offset_top = 48.0
offset_right = 1040.0
offset_bottom = 552.0
text = "You  awake. Immediately, you sense something is wrong. The ossified cradle that supports your immense form is brittle and dying. Ruptured generative organs hang around you like rotten fruit. Birthing pools froth over with stillborn progeny. Extending your senses through the vast, living hive ship that has long carried you through the stars, you realise your biomass reserves are perilously low; clearly, some cataclysm struck your vessel during your eons spent in hibernation.

Worse, your senses extend only as far as those of your ship. The greater whole to which you belong - that which this galaxy's inhabitants have in their ignorance named the Tyranid Race - is lost to you. For the first time in your existence, you are alone.

For a time, you retreat into contemplation. Dispassionately you regard the terrible wounds inflicted upon your body, the scarcity of resources, the absence of your kin. Even the genetic records you store within yourself are scrambled, inaccessible. But within them you find something of use; an old trait, inefficient, long discarded. But your kind have long memories, and in this abandoned quirk of biology you find the thinnest chance of salvation.

You have so little left. It is a calculated gamble; birthing a single viable bioform requires the cannibalisation of several of major organs, weakening you further. Finally it crawls from its birthing sac, its mind touching yours as it shakes itself clear of amniotic slime and examines the reproductive organ you have crafted for it. It is a simple thing, quicksilver-fast and hungry, its every instinct bent towards a single, overriding goal."

